                "fills": [
                  {
                    "fillColor": "#9ea3b0",
                    "fillOpacity": 1
                  }
                ],
                "fontFamily": "Inter",
                "text": "A take whose copied chains do not fit (#1515, owner's R1, 2026-10-31). A take always records and keeps its input's chain by value; when that copy would put the rig over the effects budget it comes in switched off: kept whole, saved switch on, no audio-thread time. The take plays dry until the player makes room, which matters little in the moment, so a toast in the warning amber, self-dismissing, no action (the app sends it as one line: \"GUITAR's effects are off: they don't fit with the rest of the rig. Remove an effect to turn them on.\"). Turning the chain on is refused with the over-budget message until it fits. One notice per cause: while the effects-off banner stands (see 20 \/ effects off), the take's chains join the banner and no toast is shown. Takes started together are weighed together."
              }
            ],
            "textTransform": "none",
            "textAlign": "left",
